<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea's LPMO seeking 9,613T frozen beef Friday.</title>
<headline>S.Korea's LPMO seeking 9,613T frozen beef Friday.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Livestock Products Marketing Organization (LPMO) said it would hold tenders for 9,613 tonnes of frozen beef at 2:00 p.m. (0500 GMT) on Friday.  </p>
<p>An LPMO official said acceptable origins included the United States, Canada, Ireland, Sweden, Denmark, Japan, Taiwan, New Zealand, Australia, Finland, Mexico and the Netherlands.</p>
<p>If it passes on the tenders due to high prices, the organisation will re-invite tenders on September 17, he said.</p>
<p>Arrivals were set for Seoul, Pusan, Taeku and Naju.  </p>
<p>Details for the tenders are as follow:</p>
<p>POSITION ONE (3,320 TONNES)</p>
<p>    TYPE			 TONNE     SHIPMENT</p>
<p>    Grain-fed Chuck Roll     934     Oct 15</p>
<p>    Grass-fed Fullsets	 576	  &quot;</p>
<p>    Grass-fed Bone-in	1,810	  &quot;</p>
<p>POSITION TWO (3,110 TONNES)</p>
<p>    TYPE			 TONNE     SHIPMENT</p>
<p>    Grain-fed Chuck Roll     934     Oct 25</p>
<p>    Grass-fed Fullsets	 576	  &quot;</p>
<p>    Grass-fed Bone-in	1,600	  &quot;</p>
<p>POSITION THREE (3,183 TONNES)</p>
<p>    TYPE			 TONNE     SHIPMENT</p>
<p>    Grain-fed Chuck Roll     971     Nov 5</p>
<p>    Grass-fed Fullsets	 612	 &quot;</p>
<p>    Grass-fed Bone-in	1,600	 &quot;</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5651</p>
